{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>If you see the donkey of him who hates you, etc.</b> Here כִי serves in the sense of perhaps — it is one of the four usages of the particle כִי, and this is its resolution: perhaps you will see his donkey collapsing under its load — <b>and you would refrain from leaving it with him</b> — in astonishment." "<b>You shall surely leave with him.</b> This עֲזִיבָה is a term of help; so too עָצוּר וְעָזוּב (Deuteronomy 32), and so too ״וַיַּעַזְבוּ יְרוּשָׁלַיִם עַד הַחוֹמָה״ (Nehemiah 3) — they filled it with earth to help and reinforce the strength of the wall. Similar to it: ״כִּי תֹאמַר בִּלְבָבְךָ רַבִּים הַגּוֹיִם הָאֵלֶּה מִמֶּנִּי״ etc. (Deuteronomy 7) — perhaps you will say thus, in astonishment? — ״לֹא תִירָא מֵהֶם״. And its midrash — thus our Rabbis expounded: ״כִּי תִרְאֶה״ ״וְחָדַלְתָּ״ — sometimes you refrain, and sometimes you help. How so? An old man, and it is not in keeping with his honor — you refrain; or an animal of a gentile with the load of an Israelite — you refrain (Mekhilta)." "<b>You shall surely leave with him.</b> To unload the load; מִלְּמִשְׁקַל לֵיהּ — to take the load off him."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:54:05.161341010Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}